{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# GPT Model Assembly Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `class GPTConfig` dataclass with the 124M defaults: `vocab_size=50257`, `context_length=1024`, `d_model=768`, `num_heads=12`, `num_layers=12`, `mlp_expansion=4`, `dropout=0.1`, `use_bias=True`, `weight_tying=True`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `class GPTModel` with token embedding, position embedding, embedding dropout, twelve `TransformerBlock`s, final LayerNorm, and an `lm_head` that ties to the token embedding when the flag is set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A `count_parameters` helper that returns the unique parameter count (so weight tying is honored in the count)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A `generate` function that does temperature, top-k, multinomial, and sliding window context."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that builds the model, prints the parameter count next to the reference 124M, and generates a short sequence from a fixed prompt to show the pipeline ends to end."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: parameter count alongside the 124M reference, generated token ids from a random prompt, and a confirmation that the LM head and token embedding share storage when tying is on."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "To keep the demo fast, the script also runs a tiny config (`d_model=64`, `num_layers=2`) end to end and prints the generated token sequence inline. The 124M config is built but only its parameter count and one forward pass are exercised."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Untie the LM head from the token embedding and recount parameters. Verify the delta is 50257 times 768 = 38 million.\n2. Replace the learned position embedding with a sinusoidal table computed at construction time. Confirm the model still forwards and the parameter count drops by 786,432.\n3. Add a `greedy=True` flag to generation that skips sampling and picks argmax. Confirm the sequence is deterministic across runs.\n4. Add a `repetition_penalty` knob that divides the logit of any token in the prompt or generated history by a constant before softmax. Show on a fixed prompt that values above one reduce repeat counts in the output.\n5. Add `top_p` (nucleus) sampling next to `top_k`. Two-line check that the sum of probabilities of the kept tokens exceeds `top_p`."
      ]
    }
  ],
